From 7bc9f988e85b90c58e1adc5211f2fab92acf19a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aclater <105859+aclater@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:35:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] avcodec: add PCM to DSD encoding via libdsd_upsample

libdsd_upsample converts PCM at 44.1, 88.2, 176.4 or 352.8 kHz, or at 48,
96, 192 or 384 kHz (resampled by 147/160 to the 44.1 kHz family first), to
DSD64, DSD128 or DSD256 with a delta-sigma modulator. The encoder takes
double-precision planar PCM and outputs dsd_msbf_planar packets.

As for the other DSD codecs, the sample rate of the output is the DSD bit
rate divided by 8. Since that differs from the PCM input rate, the encoder
sets avctx->sample_rate to the DSD rate in init; packet timestamps stay in
the time base chosen by the caller.

Signed-off-by: aclater <105859+aclater@users.noreply.github.com>
