+@anchor{libdsdupsample}
+@section libdsdupsample
+
+PCM to DSD (Direct Stream Digital) encoder wrapper using libdsd_upsample.
+
+The input is double-precision planar PCM at 44.1, 88.2, 176.4 or 352.8 kHz,
+or at 48, 96, 192 or 384 kHz, with 1 to 6 channels. The library resamples
+48 kHz-family input by 147/160 to the 44.1 kHz family first. The output is
+planar DSD, most significant bit first (@samp{dsd_msbf_planar}). As for the
+other DSD codecs in FFmpeg, the sample rate of the output stream is the DSD
+bit rate divided by 8.
+
+Requires the presence of the libdsd_upsample headers and library during
+configuration. You need to explicitly configure the build with
+@code{--enable-libdsdupsample}.
+
+@subsection Options
+
+@table @option
+@item dsd_rate
+Set the output rate as a multiple of 44.1 kHz. Possible values:
+@table @samp
+@item dsd64
+2.8224 MHz
+@item dsd128
+5.6448 MHz (default)
+@item dsd256
+11.2896 MHz
+@end table
+
+@item order
+Set the order of the modulator, from 5 to 8 (5 to 7 at DSD128). The default,
+@samp{auto} (-1), uses the library's default for the output rate.
+
+@item gain
+Set the gain in dB applied before the modulator, from -120 to 24.
+By default the library's default gain for DSD output is used.
+
+@item dither
+Add TPDF dither before the modulator. Default is disabled.
+@end table
+
+@subsection Examples
+Convert a WAV file to a DSD128 DSF file:
+@example
+ffmpeg -i input.wav -c:a libdsdupsample -dsd_rate dsd128 output.dsf
+@end example
+
 @anchor{libfdk-aac-enc}
 @section libfdk_aac
 
